WEBVTT

00:00:00.546 --> 00:00:02.329
This is KB Curation.

00:00:02.462 --> 00:00:04.999
It keeps the answers our chatbots give accurate,

00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:07.739
and makes sure a person approves every one of them.

00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:11.408
Here's how an answer gets from ServiceNow to the chatbot.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.686
It starts in ServiceNow.

00:00:15.249 --> 00:00:17.809
Every help article comes in with its category,

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:19.957
its state, and its flags.

00:00:20.404 --> 00:00:22.744
The states are the same as ServiceNow's:

00:00:22.784 --> 00:00:26.506
draft, in review, published, pending retirement,

00:00:26.546 --> 00:00:27.713
and retired.

00:00:28.275 --> 00:00:31.312
Internal only marks articles meant for staff,

00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:33.239
not for students or parents.

00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:39.095
Next, each category is linked to the TTU web pages its articles are

00:00:39.135 --> 00:00:40.035
based on.

00:00:40.482 --> 00:00:42.682
Those pages are checked on a schedule.

00:00:42.815 --> 00:00:45.771
When one changes, the AI reads what changed,

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:49.927
and suggests an update, a new article, or a retirement.

00:00:51.631 --> 00:00:54.459
Everything that needs a person lands in To do:

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:57.814
changes waiting for review, suggested retirements,

00:00:57.854 --> 00:01:00.089
and web pages that can't be read.

00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:04.459
Open an article to see why it was suggested,

00:01:04.499 --> 00:01:07.872
which web page it came from, and exactly what changed.

00:01:08.226 --> 00:01:10.241
The AI only suggests.

00:01:10.502 --> 00:01:12.993
Nothing changes until a person publishes it,

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.803
or sends it back to draft.

00:01:15.157 --> 00:01:18.425
And editing a published article never takes it offline.

00:01:19.828 --> 00:01:22.540
Publishing doesn't reach the chatbot on its own.

00:01:22.673 --> 00:01:24.804
When you're ready, release a version:

00:01:24.995 --> 00:01:27.730
a numbered snapshot of the whole knowledge base,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:31.015
with every article labeled with its state and flags.

00:01:31.461 --> 00:01:35.253
The chatbot reads the latest release, and shows students and parents

00:01:35.293 --> 00:01:37.923
only published articles that aren't internal.

00:01:39.709 --> 00:01:43.627
Every decision, who made it and when, is kept in History.

00:01:43.888 --> 00:01:46.925
And admins choose who can open each knowledge base.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:49.042
Import.

00:01:49.233 --> 00:01:49.959
Watch.

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:50.957
Suggest.

00:01:51.218 --> 00:01:52.049
Review.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:53.128
Release.

00:01:53.262 --> 00:01:54.905
That's KB Curation.
